# Windows development updates

- For an explicitly requested Windows build-and-install update, use `scripts/dev-install.cmd` from the repository root (PowerShell/CMD: `.\scripts\dev-install.cmd`). It only delegates to `cargo run --release --bin tomcat -- self-install` in `tomcat/`, honoring `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`.
- This updates the user's `~/.local/bin/tomcat.exe` copy, not configuration, PATH, credentials or running services. First-time PATH setup uses `tomcat init` or `self-install --add-to-path`; explicit `tomcat.path` settings and bundled extension files are not changed by this development script.
- Ordinary builds, tests and CI must not install implicitly. On macOS, use `./scripts/dev-install.sh` from the repository root in an independent terminal to build and update the standalone `~/.local/bin/tomcat` copy; it does not restart services and honors the same Agent guard.
- The platform extension automatically aligns this same user-level entry with its bundled program on every activation, without an off switch; it can replace a newer or same-version development build. Keep development binaries in their build directory and use explicit `tomcat.path` / `MULTICA_TOMCAT_PATH` (or a full terminal path) to select them. These overrides do not disable maintenance of the standard entry; bundled files are installation material, not the default runtime.
- Tomcat Agent tools carry `TOMCAT_AGENT_ACTIVE=1`; `self-install` is blocked there. Do not remove or override the guard. Offer the script command for the user's independent terminal instead; do not claim an installation happened after only building.
- Never restart the shared service through Agent Bash. After installation, the user explicitly runs `/restart` or the existing VS Code restart command (stops all tasks).
- These restrictions protect the user's installed binary, real HOME and running shared service; repository fixtures that own disposable HOME/profile/service resources may construct unmarked child environments and run directly, without changing the outer Agent marker.
